# Stage0: current249 read-only math admission

The only entry point in this packet is `preflight.py`. No action happens on
import or without `--execute`. Required invocation, with fresh values supplied
by Root:

```
.build/picocalc-apps-arm-venv/bin/python -B \
  .build/m0-math-r55-hil-20261027/operator-r1/preflight.py \
  --execute --grant ROOT_STAGE0.json --lease-sha256 EXACT_ROOT_HASH \
  --output NEW_DEDICATED_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY
```

The staged grant must be byte-identical to the live canonical
`.build/picocalc-device-handoff.json`; both hashes must match the CLI hash.
`LiveLease` checks owner, coordinator, UID, scope, stage, enabled flags, nonce,
wall expiry and a continuous budget before named open, configuration, each
select/read/write and each further response. Own FD close remains possible
after revocation. A partial write never permits continuation or a retry.
There is no global replacement of OS or port APIs. Focused tests use only an
injected inert IO instance and private authority files.

Root fields: owner=`m0-math-ram`, owner_thread=`01a14fdd-8514-7d33-b324-93b038e5f137`,
coordinator_thread=`01a164b7-9caa-7011-90d1-807e9630921c`,
uid=`E6657CD423721C35`, scope=`PICO_R55_MATH_RAM_SMOKE_ONCE`,
stage=`resident-capture`, status=`ROOT_MATH_STAGE_GO`, enabled/window/execution
flags true, 32-hex `lease_nonce`, fresh exact native `port` and `port_stat_rdev`,
`expires_unix`, `session_seconds` at most120, `max_TX_bytes` at most128,
`max_RX_bytes` at most262144, and the exact `preflight_packet_sha256` and integer `expected_physical_keys`. The first actual attempt observed cumulative25 in boot6; zero is not an assumed origin.
Root binds fresh kernel location/session/entry and no-holder evidence before
issuing it. No saved port is current authority. The supplied template is inert.

The source domain must be selected249 (`249A92DE` / `E6CFC3B8`, image1537008),
calculator stopped, service CLOSED/not dirty/empty path, no runtime/screen/disk/
M61 foreground, and an unchanged physical-key counter pinned by Root to its actual current value. KBD/PANEL/SD hardware readiness and
retained incident investigation are outside this math preflight. CRASH AVAILABLE
is recorded as source metadata; there is no crash show/clear or observer loop.

First ENQ obtains a complete source frame without pre-draining the FD. Leading
incomplete source data is preserved and rejected. After that positive idle
domain, one US resets the terminal line/enters command mode; exact banner and a
new COMMAND frame are required. Only fixed getters `identity`, `reg`, `stk`,
`hout`, `pwd`, `alarm`, `date` can be sent. Each has a fresh source-domain check
and one exact echo/prompt envelope. Input data is not replayed or changed.
No `dfu`, RAW `!`, reset, APP, SD helper, RTC setter or Flash operation exists in
this stage. Current software/watchdog diagnostics are archived from status;
scratch0..2 calendar words are not directly exposed by these read-only getters,
and the packet does not invent their values.

Outputs contain raw bytes from open, each source frame, exact getter envelopes,
current typed state/IP/settings, current RTC_SET/calendar, the direct Mach
continuous-time bracket/boot-session/timebase, and actual own-close result.
The observed zero-state rebootability is reported, never assumed. This capture
does not authorize a ROM transition or RAM launch. Root decides the next stage:
SET0 may have explicit clock HOLD after return; SET1 requires a proved time-
preserving return before launching RAM. Master13 remains separate and deferred.

All parser/revocation tests are HOST fixtures and are not current device
admission. No prior hardware acceptance, cold/PARK/UI/UART scope or lease is
reused. Actual process EXIT and fresh named no-holder adoption belong to Root.

R2 corrects only the cumulative counter admission: Root explicitly supplies the current baseline, checked on the first and every later frame in the same boot/reset epoch. The failed R1 read-only attempt remains preserved. No counter reset or additional physical key is sent.
